{"discussion":"I have all the evidence I need. The bug in compiler/unary.py is that visit_UnaryOp returns node.operand for BOTH UAdd and USub, dropping negation for all operands. The fix gates on whether the operand is an exact int/float (non-bool) Constant: UAdd returns the operand, USub returns Constant(-value), and everything else falls through to return node unchanged. I'll patch unary.py first, then incident.json, then check and submit.","operation":{"action":"patch","path":"compiler/unary.py","old":"        if isinstance(node.op, (ast.UAdd, ast.USub)):
            return ast.copy_location(node.operand, node)
        return node","new":"        if isinstance(node.op, (ast.UAdd, ast.USub)):
            if (isinstance(node.operand, ast.Constant)
                    and isinstance(node.operand.value, (int, float))
                    and not isinstance(node.operand.value, bool)):
                if isinstance(node.op, ast.UAdd):
                    return ast.copy_location(node.operand, node)
                else:
                    return ast.copy_location(ast.Constant(-node.operand.value), node)
        return node","expected_candidate_id":"28441db41e7ca5385feb03c96574fed32acfc4d67e7e608c93572fe06ed8033d","expected_file_sha256":"95544cb49ffb5b5e11f09991917e0028918e679fd7f9d164f63ea36b012d2e80"}}
